  {
   "fig_no": 1,
   "caption": "Figure 1: (Overview.) Structured SSMs independently map each channel (e.g. 퐷= 5) of an input 푥to output 푦through a higher dimensional latent state ℎ(e.g. 푁= 4). Prior SSMs avoid materializing this large eﬀective state (퐷푁, times batch size 퐵and sequence length 퐿) through clever alternate computation paths requiring time-invariance: the (∆, A, B, C) parameters are constant across time. Our selection mechanism adds back input-dependent dynamics, which also requires a careful hardware-aware algorithm to only materialize the expanded states in more eﬃcient levels of the GPU memory hierarchy.",
   "src_page": 3,
   "src_bbox": [
    72.0,
    264.11,
    561.77,
    318.71
   ],
   "trust": "A",
   "source": "official_pdf_textlayer",
